  <translations>
    <en>
      <description>Rain Bird 100-DVF is a 1″ diaphragm solenoid valve with integrated flow control. It allows manual adjustment of flow to the zone while the controller operates the water supply. The design is intended for automatic irrigation in residential gardens and professional landscape installations. DVF series specifications: operating pressure approximately 1.0–10.4 bar; flow up to about 9.1 m³/h; 24 VAC, 50/60 Hz solenoid.</description>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>b0</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>b00</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <marks>strong</marks>
          <text>100-DVF</text>
        </children>
        <children>
          <_key>b01</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text> — a 1″ diaphragm solenoid valve for automatic irrigation.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h1</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h10</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Purpose and operating principle</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p1</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p10</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>The controller energises the solenoid, which operates the diaphragm and opens the water passage. When the signal stops, the valve closes automatically. The DV/DVF series is designed for automatic irrigation in gardens and professional landscaped areas. Its diaphragm mechanism controls flow through a pilot circuit.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h2</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h20</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Construction and model-specific features</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p2</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p20</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>The model includes manual flow control. The integrated manual flow control lets the installer restrict zone flow; it does not replace hydraulic system sizing.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h3</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h30</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Hydraulic and electrical specifications</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p3</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p30</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <marks>strong</marks>
          <text>Size 1″; operating pressure 1,0–10,4 bar; flow 0,05–9,1 m³/h; solenoid 24 VAC. Actual flow depends on pipe, filter and fitting losses as well as available pressure.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h4</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h40</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Installation, adjustment and maintenance</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p4</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p40</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Connection: 1″ female thread at inlet and outlet. Before installation, confirm flow direction, operating pressure and thread standard. Fit the valve in an accessible valve box and flush the pipework before commissioning. During service, inspect the diaphragm, pilot filter, solenoid and seals. For flows below 0.68 m³/h or drip irrigation, the manufacturer recommends a 200-mesh (75 μm) upstream filter.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
